# .denylist — patterns that must never appear in this repository.
#
# Format: one Python regular expression per line. Blank lines and lines starting
# with '#' are ignored. Matching is case-insensitive and applied to every tracked
# text file. `tools/kb/denylist.py` runs the scan; CI runs it on every push. The
# scanner does not scan itself or this file (they necessarily contain the
# patterns).
#
# A rule may carry a human label after a '  ##  ' separator; the scanner prints it
# when the rule fires, so a contributor learns WHY, not just THAT.
#
# Nothing here is about hiding knowledge. It is the line between publishing a
# technique and redistributing somebody else's product. See CONTRIBUTING.md §4.

# --- protected device / vendor product names -----------------------------------
\bin[-_]?body\b                     ##  vendor product family — say "the board we worked on"
\blookin[-_]?body\b                 ##  vendor application name
\bbiospace\b                        ##  vendor name
\bdno[0-9]\b                        ##  vendor board-generation code
\blb_data\b                         ##  vendor data directory
/biospace                           ##  vendor filesystem layout

# --- unit / board serial number patterns ---------------------------------------
\bF9[0-9]{7}\b                      ##  unit serial
\bI8[0-9]{7}\b                      ##  unit serial
\bG6[0-9]{7}\b                      ##  unit serial
\bMD3D[0-9A-Z]{6,}\b                ##  main-board serial

# --- vendor secrets ------------------------------------------------------------
\bdno\b                             ##  the vendor's bootloader stop word — say "the vendor's stop word"
[A-Za-z0-9._%+-]+@xelth\.com        ##  private contact address

# --- vendor NAND / environment layout ------------------------------------------
0x0?b[08]0000\b                     ##  vendor NAND environment/mode block address
block(s)?[ ]+(88|92)\b              ##  vendor NAND block roles
bootargs[ ]+block                   ##  vendor NAND block roles

# --- file offsets inside a vendor image, quoted as product facts ----------------
0x17dec\b                           ##  offset in a vendor bootloader image
0x36450\b                           ##  offset in a vendor bootloader image
0x2fe[0-9a-f]{5}\b                  ##  vendor-image link address / offset
# Describe the CODE PATTERN a tool matches on instead, and let the tool locate the
# offset by disassembling the image the user already holds.

# --- artefacts that must not be committed at all -------------------------------
# A rule prefixed with 'path:' is matched against the FILE PATH instead of the
# file's content. (These extensions are also in .gitignore; this catches a -f add.)
path:\.(bin|dis|rom|img|elf|pdf|tgz|zip)$   ##  vendor binary / disassembly / datasheet
